  {
   "id": "gl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1588,
   "width": 826,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100054,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700378,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Not SQL indexes - the four lookup structures the operations actually depend on",
   "originalText": "Not SQL indexes - the four lookup structures the operations actually depend on",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1626,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 146,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100055,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700385,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "path -> node                    an in-memory hash map or trie keyed by the full path: the lookup every getData / setData /\n                                exists call runs. O(1), or O(path depth) - never a scan.\nthe tree structure ITSELF       serves 'list children of X' directly, because each node holds references to its immediate\n                                children by name. That is what getChildren() reads - the operation every lock,\n                                leader-election and membership recipe is built on - with no separate index to maintain.\nsessionId -> owned ephemerals   an in-memory reverse index, maintained so a session expiry deletes every ephemeral node that\n                                session owns in ONE PASS, rather than scanning the whole tree for nodes tagged with it\nwatch path -> sessions          an in-memory reverse index, purged the instant a watch fires (one-shot) or the owning session\n                                disconnects - so it never accumulates stale entries for clients long gone",
   "originalText": "path -> node                    an in-memory hash map or trie keyed by the full path: the lookup every getData / setData /\n                                exists call runs. O(1), or O(path depth) - never a scan.\nthe tree structure ITSELF       serves 'list children of X' directly, because each node holds references to its immediate\n                                children by name. That is what getChildren() reads - the operation every lock,\n                                leader-election and membership recipe is built on - with no separate index to maintain.\nsessionId -> owned ephemerals   an in-memory reverse index, maintained so a session expiry deletes every ephemeral node that\n                                session owns in ONE PASS, rather than scanning the whole tree for nodes tagged with it\nwatch path -> sessions          an in-memory reverse index, purged the instant a watch fires (one-shot) or the owning session\n                                disconnects - so it never accumulates stale entries for clients long gone",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d8",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1830,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100056,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700392,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
